### MAIN/DEV workflow (owner-decided 2026-07-19)

- **MAIN** (`:27504`, hostname `MAIN`, always-on QTV): runs the latest
  **promoted** version. A version = bot-code commit + navmesh source
  (generator sha + patch-file sha), visible in the serverinfo matchtag.
  Three bots named after their jump **with the goal in the name**:
  `tunnel-ra-10.0s`, `mega-10.0s`, `hexagon-laps` (one bot, alternating
  CCW lap then CW lap). Never experiments, never patch-polls.
  The mega drill is movement-only — rocket jumps do not count (owner
  ruling 2026-07-19; corpus-fastest grisling 3.791 is RJ and excluded,
  movement reference = Sailorman 4.865).
- **DEV** (`:27506`, hostname `DEV`): candidate version side-by-side with
  MAIN, judged on the goal metrics. Patch disk-poll lives here.
  Single-variable diagnosis rounds (same-binary A/B) also run here
  between candidates.
- **Promotion:** DEV beats/ties MAIN on all goals with no regression +
  Orchestrator review → promote: MAIN redeploys the candidate, git tag
  `stable-N` in the bot-code repo, promotion row in the planfile.
- 4th ability (RJ pentlift→window) joins the roster later.
- **Benchwall (owner-ordered 2026-07-19):** live bench page at
  `benchwall/` — 3 MAIN POVs over 3 DEV POVs (hub qtv-popout iframes)
  with goal/corpus/best/streak-of-10 stats per screen, plus a BIG focus
  area. Screen ids `main1..3`, `dev1..3`, `BIG` are canonical vocabulary
  (registry: `benchwall/screens.json`) — used in HTML badges, driver
  artifacts, reports and planfile rows. Bot name prefix is `MAIN`/`DEV`
  (caps, colored QW chars), NOT `bot`; renames/goal changes ship as one
  delivery (screens.json + planfile row + serverside rename at a round
  boundary). After every run the driver refreshes
  `benchwall/data/scoreboard.json` (+ history.jsonl). Full spec:
  `docs/plans/2026-07-19-benchwall-spec.md`. Auditor builds & keeps the
  page consistent; Operator owns the data plane and in-game names.
- **Stock movement parity (hard owner rule):** MOD abilities are OFF for
  all human-comparison work — `rtx_doublejump 0`, `rtx_walljump 0`,
  grapple/RJ mod-toggles 0. NEVER trust code defaults (`rtx_walljump`
