### Interaction contract (all seats)

1. Blocker → diagnosis with exact coordinates/data (Operator) → fix in
   the owning lane (worker) → independent review (Orchestrator) →
   deploy → A/B verdict (Operator). No step skipped, no self-judging.
2. Every claim ships with evidence: test output, sha, screenshot, or
   artifact row. "Done" without evidence is not done.
3. One heavy build (~100 CPU-min) machine-wide at a time — announce in
   the planfile before starting.
4. Negative results are pinned as tests, not deleted.
5. Mentioning a home server/match ⇒ include the QTV link.
6. Patch/overlay exports reach disk only AFTER (or together with) their
   planfile row — DEV's disk-poll applies them live, so a silent export
   is a silent deploy.
7. Live round artifacts (loop-jsonl) are NOT committed while growing:
   gitignored during the round, rotated per round and committed at
   round end.
8. Planfile rows are appended via `ops/planlog.py` (correct timestamp +
   seat signature; pass `--file` explicitly until planfile rotation
   lands). Patch exports go through `planlog export` so the row is
   durable on disk BEFORE the patch reaches its polled destination.
9. Heavy builds run via `ops/heavy.sh --seat <name> -- <cmd>` (machine-
   wide flock + auto announce/done rows + containment env). A held lock
   means WAIT, not retry. Parity readback comes from
   `ops/parity_readback.py --server MAIN|DEV` (paste its output line;
   it self-refuses with exit 2 while a driver holds the control lock —
   run it in driver gaps or let the driver emit the line).
10. A judged round's criteria may be amended mid-round by an Orchestrator
   planfile row when forensics has already settled a criterion — don't
   spend drive time measuring a settled question.
9. Claims built on filtered artifact data are re-checked against the
   raw artifact before they become an order to another seat.
10. Any graph analysis must cite the live-graph facit sha + kind counts
   verified against the server's navmesh log line (regenerate with
   `ops/dump_live_graph.py`). Analysis against a facit without a parity
   proof is invalid — the old offline nav_dump (33920 links, no entity
   data) misled a full patch campaign on 2026-07-19.

