## The CLIs (all print JSON)

Prefix every command with the WSL wrapper above (`uv run ...` from the repo).

### dm3-route-report — the owner's route questions in ONE command

When the owner points out a route, run this first:

```bash
uv run dm3-route-report tunnel-to-ra --top 5
uv run dm3-route-report quad-to-ra --no-combat --check-archive
uv run dm3-route-report tunnel-to-ra --publish median   # -> Route Lab catalog
```

One JSON answer: median + fastest (whole cohort AND frag-free), a concrete
MEDIAN EXEMPLAR run and the fastest runs with player/demo identity, demo
availability in the existing channels (hub via HTTP; `--check-archive` also
ssh-checks servexeri's 4on4-corpus archive), and ready-to-run `dm3-deeplink`
+ `dm3-viewer-catalog` commands per run.  `--publish median|fastest` writes
the catalog entry directly.  Builds the cohort automatically when missing.

### dm3-cohort — route benchmarks in milliseconds

Routes live in `route_lab/routes_dm3.json` (owner names; start = exact spawn
point(s), an item take, or a `crossing` — a downward z-plane crossing inside
an XY box, e.g. dropping through a floor hole; target = item, optional
`origin` for multi-instance items like mh).  Adding a route = adding a JSON
stanza;
semantics (exact binding, target active at start, first global take,
same-life, <= max_s) are generated identically to the pinned gate SQL and
regression-tested against it.

```bash
uv run dm3-cohort routes                     # list registered routes
uv run dm3-cohort build --route tunnel-to-ra # once per corpus version (~2 min)
uv run dm3-cohort stats --route tunnel-to-ra # whole cohort: n/median/fastest
uv run dm3-cohort stats --route tunnel-to-ra --player milton --no-combat
uv run dm3-cohort runs --route tunnel-to-ra --no-combat --limit 10
```

`--no-combat` = frag-free (obituary level; damage-without-frag is invisible in
this corpus - always state that caveat when reporting "no combat").

### dm3-viewer-catalog — the "Manuellt valda" category on routes.html

```bash
uv run dm3-viewer-catalog add --demo-sha <sha> --slot 2 --t0 1087965 --t1 1097030 \
    --label "Tunnel → RA · Milton 9.065 s (combat-fri)" --route-id manual-milton-tunnel-to-ra
uv run dm3-viewer-catalog list
uv run dm3-viewer-catalog validate
uv run dm3-viewer-catalog remove --route-id <id>
```

Catalog: `qw-analyzer/dist/routes/dm3-manual-picks.json`, rendered by
`http://127.0.0.1:4173/routes.html` (Datakälla → "Manuellt valda"). `add`
validates before writing (schema, monotonic times, pitch range, teleport
detection) and refuses to write a broken catalog.

### dm3-deeplink — watchable hub link for a run

Windows-side (needs ssh to servexeri + local mvd-api):

```bash
uv run dm3-deeplink --sha <demo_id> --name "<orig_name>" --at 1087.9 --track milton
```

Resolves the demo (hub folder, else servexeri `4on4-corpus` archive), rebuilds
the hub index, resolves the FTE userid via mvd-api, prints LAN + Tailscale
player URLs seeked 5 s before the moment. Run it from Windows (ssh keys +
wsl.exe are assumed), the others from WSL.

