plugins/qw-bot-control/skills/operate-qw-bot-lab/references/control-contract.md:14:| `status`, `server_log` | Read managed server/navmesh/bot state |
plugins/qw-bot-control/skills/operate-qw-bot-lab/references/control-contract.md:17:| `goto` | Production path execution to a coordinate; ends in `arrived` or `goto_stall` |
plugins/qw-bot-control/skills/operate-qw-bot-lab/references/control-contract.md:27:The current game parser recognizes `status`, `links`, `prep`, `teleport`, `goto`, `rj`, `fly`, `hold`, `stop`, `ra_trial`, `set`, `get`, `cmd`, `cell`, `route`, `curls`, `probe`, `curl`, `planlink`, `planrj`, `planrjraw`, and `unlink`. Not all are exposed by rjtune. Use checked-in route-lab drivers for special drills rather than inventing a wire client.
plugins/qw-bot-control/skills/operate-qw-bot-lab/references/control-contract.md:41:Water behavior exists in production: graph cells carry water/breathability state, bhop is suppressed in water, submerged bots hold swim-up when needed, and anti-drown routing seeks a breathable cell. Unit coverage is supporting evidence only; require a live drill before calling the capability validated.
