index 04f4ccec470660ff7d40aa91bdc5b9c07dbfec47..34316d85ca4adcf92da32c51c15a9c6d46be5843
--- a/C:/Users/benya/projects/quakeworld/route-lab-viewer-live/qw-nav-viewer/RUNBOOK.md
+++ b/C:/Users/benya/projects/quakeworld/route-lab-viewer-live/qw-nav-viewer/RUNBOOK.md
@@ -239,10 +239,31 @@
   "map": "dm3",
   "grid": 32.0,
   "cells": [[448.0, 192.0, 56.0]],
-  "links": [[0, 1, "Walk", 0.1]]
+  "cell_ids": [4711],
+  "links": [[0, 1, "Walk", 0.1]],
+  "link_ids": [50259]
 }
 ```
 
+`cell_ids` and `link_ids` are optional parallel arrays used by the live viewer.
+Their lengths must match `cells`/`links`, and every ID must be unique. A
+mismatch or duplicate leaves the static graph usable but disables both live-ID
+maps and emits a console warning. Link kinds are parsed case-insensitively and
+normalized to the canonical spelling above.
+
+### Live fasttrack layer
+
+Add `?graph=<name>&live=<port>` to connect directly to
+`ws://127.0.0.1:<port>`. Without `live`, no WebSocket is created and static
+behavior is unchanged. Live frames use `qw-live-frame/1`; their 16-character
+graph SHA-256 fingerprint must match the exact fetched graph bytes. A mismatch
+shows `live: graph mismatch` and draws no live layer.
+
+Matching frames add two retained buffers without rebuilding the static graph:
+bright active/dim used cells in the surface buffer, and yellow-to-red used
+links plus an axis-aligned bot box in the line buffer. Press `L` to toggle
+follow-camera for the first bot in each frame. `F` remains frame-map.
+
 Traversal-aware dumps may add `speed_jump_payloads`, `speed_jump_traversals`, and
 `speed_jump_traversal_provenance`. Rendering ignores those sidecars, while audit tools use them to
 bind a displayed link to its payload or `SpeedJumpTraversal`, ground-turn contract, launchbox,
